WEBVTT

00:00:00.617 --> 00:00:05.044
Welcome to Portfolio Tracker This guide explains the Import screen

00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:08.208
and the Manage Portfolios screen We will walk through the

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:11.815
recommended brokerage import order look closely at the Charles Schwab

00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:15.995
workflow explain the Generic Import choices and then set up

00:00:15.995 --> 00:00:21.294
accounts Owner and aggregates You can create as many individual

00:00:21.294 --> 00:00:26.034
accounts or portfolios as you need Those accounts remain independent

00:00:26.464 --> 00:00:29.185
and you can combine any selection of them in one

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:31.620
or more aggregate views whenever you want

00:00:33.364 --> 00:00:36.437
Start on Broker Import The screen is designed to be

00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:40.539
used in order First import a current Positions export That

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:44.341
establishes the current shares and cost basis for the selected

00:00:44.354 --> 00:00:50.526
account Next import Transaction History That adds purchases sales dividends

00:00:50.786 --> 00:00:56.489
reinvestments and lots after the positions snapshot exists Last Refresh

00:00:56.658 --> 00:00:59.796
is optional Use it when you want the latest prices

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.184
and forward-looking dividend fields A positions file is a full

00:01:04.198 --> 00:01:07.713
current snapshot so use a complete export rather than a

00:01:07.726 --> 00:01:11.671
partial file The other tabs are for broker-neutral spreadsheets a

00:01:11.685 --> 00:01:15.682
combined app export or a Snowball migration not the normal

00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:16.489
broker path

00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:21.955
For a single Charles Schwab account go to Accounts then

00:01:21.955 --> 00:01:25.913
Positions in Schwab and export the current view to CSV

00:01:26.031 --> 00:01:31.018
or Excel Back in Portfolio Tracker choose Charles Schwab leave

00:01:31.018 --> 00:01:35.028
the workflow on Positions and choose This account The import

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:39.572
reads the holdings shares cost basis and current prices from

00:01:39.572 --> 00:01:42.645
that export You can download the Schwab template when you

00:01:42.645 --> 00:01:46.447
need the exact field names Choose the file set the

00:01:46.551 --> 00:01:50.940
NAV snapshot date if needed and select Preview Review the

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:54.169
rows before you confirm the import This is the step

00:01:54.286 --> 00:01:58.309
that makes the account holdings match the complete broker snapshot

00:02:00.054 --> 00:02:04.247
Schwab can also export Positions for All Accounts In Schwab

00:02:04.703 --> 00:02:08.023
switch the account selector to All Accounts before exporting the

00:02:08.023 --> 00:02:12.398
CSV or Excel file On this screen choose Charles Schwab

00:02:12.671 --> 00:02:17.294
Positions then All Accounts The preview separates the export into

00:02:17.294 --> 00:02:20.770
account blocks and lists your portfolios that are tagged Charles

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:24.976
Schwab on Manage Portfolios Check only the portfolios you want

00:02:24.976 --> 00:02:29.052
to update You can verify or change each mapping before

00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:32.554
anything is written skip an account in the file or

00:02:32.554 --> 00:02:37.007
create a destination portfolio for a new account Confirmed routing

00:02:37.138 --> 00:02:41.187
is remembered for the next combined export This shortcut is

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.341
for Positions transaction history is still imported one account at

00:02:45.341 --> 00:02:45.731
a time

00:02:47.471 --> 00:02:51.859
After the positions import choose Transactions in the same workflow

00:02:52.276 --> 00:02:56.443
In Schwab go to Accounts then History choose the date

00:02:56.443 --> 00:03:00.622
range you need and export the Transactions CSV or Excel

00:03:00.635 --> 00:03:04.151
file Preview it and then import it into that one

00:03:04.359 --> 00:03:09.646
selected account This adds transaction history such as buys sells

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:15.687
dividend payments and DRIP reinvestments Importing positions first matters it

00:03:15.687 --> 00:03:19.125
preserves the current broker holdings while the history is added

00:03:19.125 --> 00:03:24.424
behind them Reimporting an older history file safely skips matching

00:03:24.424 --> 00:03:28.956
transaction rows and duplicate dividend payments When a file is

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:32.849
incomplete use the review screen before confirming so you do

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:36.312
not mistake a partial history for the entire account record

00:03:38.054 --> 00:03:41.778
The other broker choices work the same basic way Select

00:03:41.778 --> 00:03:44.942
the broker that supplied the export start with its current

00:03:44.955 --> 00:03:48.888
Positions file for the selected account then import its Transaction

00:03:48.888 --> 00:03:54.877
History and optionally refresh prices and dividend data E*TRADE Fidelity

00:03:55.151 --> 00:03:59.278
Robinhood and Interactive Brokers each have their matching format and

00:03:59.526 --> 00:04:03.914
downloadable template or field guidance on the screen Interactive Brokers

00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:08.484
uses its Activity Statement for positions and its Transaction History

00:04:08.497 --> 00:04:13.236
export for activity Fidelity also offers an optional All Accounts

00:04:13.236 --> 00:04:17.989
positions shortcut that uses the same preview-and-map approach as Schwab

00:04:18.393 --> 00:04:23.445
Regardless of broker the important sequence is unchanged a complete

00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:28.536
current positions snapshot first activity history second and a preview

00:04:28.549 --> 00:04:29.877
before the final import

00:04:31.624 --> 00:04:34.632
Choose Generic Positions when your data is in your own

00:04:34.645 --> 00:04:37.991
spreadsheet or another source that does not match a brokerage

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:42.158
importer The minimum columns are Ticker and Shares You can

00:04:42.158 --> 00:04:47.588
also provide Price Paid Dividend Frequency Ex-Dividend Date and DRIP

00:04:48.017 --> 00:04:51.442
Use Download Holdings Template to begin with the supported layout

00:04:51.872 --> 00:04:55.491
The app enriches eligible holdings with market data If the

00:04:55.491 --> 00:05:00.687
selected portfolio already has positions Generic Import uses merge mode

00:05:01.155 --> 00:05:05.049
it updates matching tickers and adds new ones while preserving

00:05:05.062 --> 00:05:08.929
app-only values such as DRIP or pay dates unless your

00:05:08.929 --> 00:05:12.939
spreadsheet supplies them You can also import all filled workbook

00:05:12.939 --> 00:05:17.431
tabs as separate portfolios which is useful for a multi-account

00:05:17.431 --> 00:05:18.056
spreadsheet

00:05:19.794 --> 00:05:24.664
Generic Transactions is the companion to Generic Positions Use its

00:05:24.755 --> 00:05:29.482
XLSX or CSV format for one row per BUY SELL

00:05:29.703 --> 00:05:35.159
DIVIDEND DRIP deposit withdrawal or share transfer It uses the

00:05:35.159 --> 00:05:41.135
same preview duplicate protection and realized-gain workflow as broker transaction

00:05:41.148 --> 00:05:46.513
imports Positions plus Transactions is different it restores one workbook

00:05:46.526 --> 00:05:50.185
that contains both a portfolio sheet and a Transactions sheet

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:53.870
such as a workbook exported by this app. Its scope

00:05:53.883 --> 00:05:58.740
controls can import both sections together or run positions only

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:02.815
or transactions only Match the tab to the file A

00:06:02.815 --> 00:06:07.867
combined workbook belongs on Positions plus Transactions while a normal

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.120
broker export belongs on Broker Import

00:06:11.874 --> 00:06:16.093
Now open Manage Portfolios Each regular row is a real

00:06:16.405 --> 00:06:20.963
independent portfolio or brokerage account Use New Portfolio whenever you

00:06:20.963 --> 00:06:24.127
want another account there is no fixed limit Give it

00:06:24.127 --> 00:06:28.215
a meaningful name choose the appropriate broker source before importing

00:06:28.684 --> 00:06:32.642
and it keeps its own holdings transaction history cash snapshot

00:06:33.072 --> 00:06:36.718
and settings The table lets you rename an account inline

00:06:37.122 --> 00:06:39.895
select it as the active account or move it up

00:06:39.908 --> 00:06:43.593
and down in the portfolio selector Add accounts for every

00:06:43.606 --> 00:06:49.049
brokerage retirement account experiment household member or separate strategy you

00:06:49.062 --> 00:06:52.747
want to track Creating another account does not merge it

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.439
with any existing account

00:06:56.204 --> 00:06:59.277
The Broker Source is the broker whose importer is allowed

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.636
to write to that portfolio it is independent of the

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:07.064
account name Account Type marks a portfolio User-owned or Test

00:07:07.077 --> 00:07:11.920
/ non-owned Test accounts remain usable but cannot be included

00:07:11.933 --> 00:07:15.553
in Owner Show controls whether an account appears in the

00:07:15.553 --> 00:07:20.215
top portfolio selector Clearing Show simply hides it there it

00:07:20.228 --> 00:07:24.173
does not delete data Cash is a dated snapshot not

00:07:24.173 --> 00:07:27.832
a live balance Click a regular account’s cash amount to

00:07:27.897 --> 00:07:32.324
update it manually broker imports can replace it later The

00:07:32.324 --> 00:07:36.855
arrows set display order and Select changes the active account

00:07:37.259 --> 00:07:42.025
Clear removes holdings and the transaction ledger Reset also removes

00:07:42.038 --> 00:07:46.204
option trades and the DRIP contribution schedule and Delete removes

00:07:46.217 --> 00:07:49.746
the portfolio itself after a confirmation and backup

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:54.069
Owner is optional Create it only when you want a

00:07:54.082 --> 00:07:58.288
personal rollup of selected user-owned brokerage accounts Then use the

00:07:58.301 --> 00:08:02.819
Owner checkbox on each regular user-owned account to include or

00:08:02.819 --> 00:08:06.309
exclude it Owner does not turn those accounts into one

00:08:06.322 --> 00:08:10.645
database record each account stays independent and keeps its own

00:08:10.658 --> 00:08:14.603
broker import destination Owner itself is never a place to

00:08:14.603 --> 00:08:19.720
import a broker file Instead import each brokerage file into

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.379
its matching regular account and the checked accounts feed the

00:08:23.392 --> 00:08:28.327
Owner rollup The Dashboard uses this configuration for Owner-level income

00:08:28.575 --> 00:08:33.900
and DRIP-versus-cash calculations Test or non-owned accounts cannot be checked

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.262
for Owner so temporary portfolios stay out of a personal

00:08:38.262 --> 00:08:39.239
rollup by design

00:08:41.014 --> 00:08:44.881
Aggregates are separate from Owner An aggregate is a read-only

00:08:44.881 --> 00:08:49.686
virtual portfolio that combines the real portfolios you check as

00:08:49.686 --> 00:08:54.400
members Click Add Aggregate rename it and choose its member

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.525
accounts You can make as many aggregates as you want

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:02.082
one for every account one for a household one for

00:09:02.082 --> 00:09:05.741
retirement accounts or one for a strategy There is no

00:09:05.754 --> 00:09:10.272
one-to-one rule The same individual account can be included in

00:09:10.415 --> 00:09:14.348
any number of aggregates and every aggregate can use any

00:09:14.361 --> 00:09:19.087
combination of the available regular portfolios Owner itself is not

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.941
an aggregate member Each aggregate has its own Show checkbox

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:28.332
ordering arrows Select button and Delete button Deleting an aggregate

00:09:28.345 --> 00:09:33.241
removes only the virtual definition it never removes the underlying

00:09:33.241 --> 00:09:34.894
accounts or their data

00:09:36.618 --> 00:09:41.006
To recap create a regular portfolio for every real account

00:09:41.006 --> 00:09:43.519
you want to track tag it with the matching broker

00:09:43.519 --> 00:09:48.324
source and import a complete positions snapshot before transaction history

00:09:48.741 --> 00:09:52.113
Use Generic Import when your spreadsheet is not a supported

00:09:52.113 --> 00:09:55.759
broker export Create Owner only for the personal rollup you

00:09:55.772 --> 00:09:59.808
want and use aggregates for any other combinations You can

00:09:59.808 --> 00:10:03.363
add more accounts at any time keep them independent and

00:10:03.376 --> 00:10:06.996
place the same account into any combination of aggregate views

00:10:07.412 --> 00:10:12.256
Review previews before imports and read the Clear Reset and

00:10:12.256 --> 00:10:17.959
Delete confirmations carefully For informational purposes only Not financial advice
